{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-307197-r4612001","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Fish Biryani","sourcePageId":307197,"sourceRevision":"4612001","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-01-16T07:24:08Z","sourceRevisionUser":"A Sulaiman Z","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Fish%20Biryani&oldid=4612001","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:41:53.340Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Cookbook pages needing work","Category:Incomplete recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using fish","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"01addafa7ee3086828c246fc35ec606bc851c505adb47d66864bb65bfcf8afb0","sourceWikitext":"{{Incomplete recipe}}{{cookwork|unclear relationship between ingredients and directions}}{{recipesummary|category=Fish recipes|servings=6–8|time=120 minutes|difficulty=1\n}}{{recipe}}\n\n'''Fish biryani''' is a dish from Cape Malay, South Africa.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Marinade ===\n* 8 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* 2–3 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] fresh ground red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chillies]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Cilantro|crushed dhania]] ([[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]]) seeds\n* 1–2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] crushed jeera ([[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]]) seeds\n* Juice of 1 [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]] \n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]] \n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato puree]]\n\n=== Biryani ===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]] [[Cookbook:Fish|fish]] filets\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] uncooked [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]] \n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] masoor (red or pink [[Cookbook:Lentil|lentils]])\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Onions|onions]], grated\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]], grated\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]]  [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]] \n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook: Clarified Butter|ghee]]\n* 8 small  [[Cookbook:Potatoes|potatoes]] \n* Few [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]], whole peppers, tuj pieces\n* 4 whole [[Cookbook:Chiles|green chillies]]\n* 4 elachi ([[Cookbook:Cardamom|green cardamom]]) pods\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] jeera ([[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]])\n* 1/2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook: Turmeric|turmeric]]\n* [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Yoghurt|yoghurt]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Pound garlic and chiles together to make a paste. Mix in the coriander, cumin, lemon juice, turmeric, salt, oil, and tomato purée to make marinade.\n# Smear fish filets with the marinade. Refrigerate for 1 hour.\n# Boil the rice and the masoor separately until cooked.\n# Fry [[Cookbook:Onions|onions]] in the ½ cup [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]] until golden in color. Strain out extra oil.\n# Combine strained onion oil with ghee. Heat, this and use to fry the patties. Keep aside oils in which onions etc. were fried.\n# Fry [[Cookbook:Fish|fish]] in separate oil\n# In a deep bowl add yoghurt, grated tomato, spices and fried onions ( reserve 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] of onion for top of rice). Dip fried fish in the marinade for a few minutes. I a large flat bottomed pot, pour the oils that were left aside in which excess oil was poured, add the remaining ghee and oil, the sprinkle some masoor over it.\n# Arrange fish slices and all marinade over masoor and oil/ghee. Cover with rest of masoor.\n# Arrange patties over masoor and finally cover the rice. Sprinkle top of rice with the reserved fried onion and hot with ghee.\n# Sprinkle 1/4 cup water over rice, close lid tightly and put on heat. when pot starts sizzling lower heat and simmer for 30-40 minutes.\n\n== Notes & Tricks==\nOn no account must the oil used for frying the fish be used in biryani.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using fish]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Fish Biryani","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"8 cloves garlic","sourceText":"8 cloves garlic","amountText":"8 cloves garlic","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2–3 teaspoons fresh ground red chillies","sourceText":"2–3 teaspoons fresh ground red chillies","amountText":"2–3 teaspoons fresh ground red chillies","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 teaspoon crushed dhania (coriander) seeds","sourceText":"1 teaspoon crushed dhania (coriander) seeds","amountText":"1 teaspoon crushed dhania (coriander) seeds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1–2 teaspoon crushed jeera (cumin) seeds","sourceText":"1–2 teaspoon crushed jeera (cumin) seeds","amountText":"1–2 teaspoon crushed jeera (cumin) seeds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Juice of 1 lemon","sourceText":"Juice of 1 lemon","amountText":"Juice of 1 lemon","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 teaspoon turmeric","sourceText":"1 teaspoon turmeric","amountText":"1 t